    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 14,
      "title": "Traces (Jaeger)",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 31
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": 15,
      "title": "Follow a change",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 32
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Every input becomes one trace: `source.publish` \u2192 `query.process` \u2192 `sink.handle` (the Debug profile adds `query.evaluate`, `query.commit` and other phases), with `instance_id`, `graph_id` and `component_id` attributes.\n\n- The Grafana link printed by `demo.sh showcase` opens one real input trace below.\n- To follow another change, pick a trace in the [Jaeger UI](http://127.0.0.1:16686/search?service=drasi-server-observability) (default port; the script prints the actual link) and paste its ID into **Trace ID** above.\n- Grafana's bundled Jaeger data source opens traces by ID but cannot *search* Jaeger 2.21+ (grafana/grafana-jaeger-datasource#87), so search in the Jaeger UI."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "traces",
      "id": 16,
      "title": "Trace ${trace_id}",
      "description": "The trace whose ID is entered in the Trace ID box, read through the Jaeger data source.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "jaeger",
        "uid": "drasi-jaeger"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 16,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 37
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "jaeger",
            "uid": "drasi-jaeger"
          },
          "query": "${trace_id}"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
